Key optimizations:

Single #pragma omp parallel region spans all reps, avoiding per-iteration fork/join overhead across the 20 reps.

Each rep is an omp for (implicit barrier ensures all writes to y from rep r are visible before rep r+1 reads them — required for correctness since each rep depends on the previous one through y).

schedule(static) gives each thread a contiguous chunk, matching the memory-bound access pattern and minimizing false sharing/scheduling overhead.

Correctness is preserved: results are bit-identical to the serial version because each element's chain of reps dependent updates is performed in the same order, just distributed across threads by element.
